{"name":"Indian Patties","permalink":"indian-patties","edit":"https://github.com/The-Silverwood-Institute/Recibase/tree/master/src/main/scala/se/reciba/api/recibase/recipes/IndianPatties.scala","source":"Vegetarian Cookery Bible (2012: Reader's Digest)","description":"Vegetarian burger patties made with red lentils, spinach, mint and spices.","tagline":null,"notes":["Work well served with sweet chilli sauce and/or mayonnaise.","Don't waste time finely chopping the ingredients as they're blended anyway.","If you don't have a blender you can chop the garlic, chilli and ginger finely then cook the onion at the same time.","Can take a long time."],"dated_notes":[],"tags":["Vegetarian","High Effort","Slow","Spicy"],"inherited_tags":["Pescatarian","Vegetarian-ish"],"image":null,"ingredients_blocks":[{"name":null,"ingredients":[{"name":"Red lentils","quantity":"225g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Whole cloves","quantity":"1-2","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Coriander seeds","quantity":"2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":"Or ground coriander"},{"name":"Cumin seeds","quantity":"1-2 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Black peppercorns","quantity":"1 tsp","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Garlic","quantity":"2-3 cloves","prep":"chopped or crushed","notes":null},{"name":"Ginger","quantity":"1cm piece","prep":"peeled and chopped/grated","notes":null},{"name":"Onion","quantity":"1","prep":"diced","notes":null},{"name":"Spinach","quantity":"225g","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Coriander leaves","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Mint leaves","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Chillies","quantity":"1-2","prep":"chopped, seeds removed if desired","notes":null},{"name":"Ground cinnamon","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Egg","quantity":"1","prep":null,"notes":null},{"name":"Salt","quantity":null,"prep":null,"notes":null}]}],"method":["Set the lentils aside in boiling water to soften.","Meanwhile, dry-roast the cloves, cumin seeds, coriander seeds and black peppercorns in a pan. Grid thoroughly with a mortar and pestle and set aside.","Add the chillies, garlic and ginger to the pan with a little oil and soften. Add the (drained) lentils, along with the spinach, coriander and mint and cook for 5-10 minutes.","Add the ground spices, cinnamon, egg and salt and mix.","Blend the mixture thoroughly.","Add the onion and pulse blender until finely chopped but not pureed.","Form the mixture into ~5cm patties and brush with oil on both sides.","Place them on a baking tray under the grill until brown and crisp on both sides, turning as necessary.","Serve hot."]}